# --- the LingBot-VA policy server -------------------------------------------
# This is env.sh's IWM_SERVER_PY (formerly a hand-rolled /home/ubuntu/.venv-lingbot).
# Versions are lingbot-va/requirements.txt exactly, because the server has to be
# the upstream one -- InstinctWM patches it at runtime and measures the delta, so
# a drifted baseline is a mismeasured optimization.
#
# WHY THIS IS A SEPARATE FILE AND NOT A pyproject.toml DEPENDENCY-GROUP.
# uv builds one universal lockfile for the project. torch==2.9.0 below satisfies
# the `runtime` extra's torch>=2.4, so if these pins lived in pyproject.toml uv
# would resolve a single torch for both and the development environments would be
# silently dragged down to the server's version (measured: runtime alone picks
# 2.13.0; with the server in the same lock, 2.9.0). `[tool.uv] conflicts` does not
# prevent this -- it constrains what may be INSTALLED together, not what is
# RESOLVED together. Keeping the server in its own file, locked separately, is
# what makes the two solves actually independent. See env.sh: "Never try to merge
# these."
#
# Regenerate the lock after editing:
#   ./scripts/task.sh lock-server
#
# TWO DELIBERATE OMISSIONS from lingbot-va/requirements.txt:
#
#  * flash_attn. RESULTS.md's appendix: with a real flash-attn wheel installed,
#    diffusers detects it via package METADATA and routes autoencoder_kl_wan down
#    a flash-attention path instead of SDPA, changing the VAE's numerics. The
#    91.6% baseline was measured with no real flash-attn, so installing one is not
#    a free environment change -- it invalidates the baseline. The transformer
#    never calls it (attn_mode='torch' -> custom_sdpa); it is an unused
#    module-scope import, which is what IWM_FA_SHIM=1 covers.
#  * lerobot / scipy / wandb. requirements.txt marks these "# Post-training".
#    Serving and evaluating never import them.

torch==2.9.0
torchvision==0.24.0
torchaudio==2.9.0
diffusers==0.36.0
transformers==4.55.2
numpy==1.26.4
accelerate
einops
easydict
tqdm
imageio[ffmpeg]
websockets
msgpack
opencv-python
matplotlib
ftfy
safetensors
pillow
